<body style="height: auto; min-height: auto;">Ref No: {{{Case.Case_Number__c}}}<br />
<br />
Hi {{{Case.First_Name__c}}},<br />
<br />
Thank you for notifying Qantas of your mobility aid.<br />
<br />
There are size restrictions and requirements for the carriage of mobility aids, depending on the aircraft type operating. You must check the maximum dimensions against your own wheelchair dimensions prior to travel.<br />
<br />
Our records indicate, the dimensions of your wheelchair <strong>width cm / height cm / length cm</strong> exceed the maximum dimensions excepted on a <strong>737 / 787 / 330 / 380 / 717 / DASH 8 / 190 / 100</strong>.<br />
<br />
Please contact us to discuss the details of your mobility aid to process your booking.<br />
<br />
<strong>Powered wheelchairs/ mobility aids</strong><br />
In accordance with manufacturer's recommendations and to reduce any risk of damage to your mobility aid, all electric wheelchairs, including power assist wheelchairs, must travel in the upright position (folded or unfolded) in the free wheel mode. To facilitate this requirement, check the <a href="https://www.qantas.com/au/en/travel-info/specific-needs/mobility-assistance.html#maximum-dimensions">maximum dimensions</a> to ensure we can accept your mobility aid/s on our aircraft.<br />
<br />
<strong>Manual wheelchairs/ mobility aids</strong><br />
All manual wheelchairs must fit within the <a href="https://www.qantas.com/au/en/travel-info/specific-needs/mobility-assistance.html#maximum-dimensions">maximum dimensions</a> in the upright position (folded or unfolded). If the wheelchair fits within the <a href="https://www.qantas.com/au/en/travel-info/specific-needs/mobility-assistance.html#maximum-dimensions">maximum dimensions</a> but not in the upright position, the wheelchair can only be carried if it weighs less than 32 kgs and the manufacturer has confirmed that the wheelchair can be stored and transported on its side. Otherwise, the wheelchair must fit within the <a href="https://www.qantas.com/au/en/travel-info/specific-needs/mobility-assistance.html#maximum-dimensions">maximum dimensions</a> in the upright position to be carried.<br />
<br />
If you require further assistance with your mobility aid, please reply back to this email or contact the Qantas Customer Specific Needs team between 6am and 10pm (AEST), Monday to Sunday on 1800 177 474 (within Australia) or +61 2 9123 7471 (outside Australia) on 1800 177 474, option 3.</body>
</html>